   138	**Proof.** Scale c to an integer vector C by a common positive denominator D; compare C·x with DK. For n coordinates put B=2^n and q_i=B C_i+2^(i-1), i=1,...,n. The binary code sum_i 2^(i-1)x_i lies between 0 and B-1 and is distinct for different binary x. Hence q has a unique minimizer whenever F is nonempty, and that minimizer also minimizes C: a change of at least 1 in C·x dominates the entire tie-breaking code. All q_i have polynomial encoding length.
