   148	Any deterministic algorithm deciding whether F is empty needs 2^n queries in the worst case. Indeed, until every point has been queried, the transcript consisting entirely of negative answers is consistent both with the empty set and with a singleton at any unqueried point. With a nonempty-singleton promise, finding s requires at least 2^n-1 queries in the worst case, since two unqueried candidates remain indistinguishable before that many queries.
