   826	Theorem 1. (Grötschel et al. [1993]) Let P ⊆ Rn be a polyhedron with facet complexity ϕ. Given an oracle
   827	for any one of
   828	
   829	   • the dual bound verification problem over P with linear objective coefficient d ∈ Qn ,
   830	   • the separation problem for P with respect to x̂ ∈ Qn , or
   831	   • the primal bound verification problem for P with linear objective coefficient d ∈ Qn ,
   832	
   833	there exists an oracle polynomial-time algorithm for solving either of the other two problems. Further, all
   834	three problems are solvable in time polynomial in n, ϕ, and either hdi (in the case of primal or dual bound
   835	verification) or hx̂i (in the case of separation).
   836	
   837	The problem of verifying a given dual bound was called the violation problem by Grötschel et al. [1993]. The
   838	above result refers only to the facet complexity ϕ, but we could also replace it with the vertex complexity ν,
   839	since it is easy to show that ν ≤ 4n2 ϕ. In the remainder of the paper, we refer to the “polyhedral complexity”
   840	whenever the facet complexity and vertex complexity can be used interchangeably.
